 "text": "Here's a new feature: narrated whiteboard mode. You write one scene file, with boxes, arrows and narration. The solver lays everything out and times it, and Kokoro turns the script into a voice, with a timestamp for every word. Then the same scene goes two ways: to a video, or to a live canvas, where each shape is drawn exactly as its word is spoken. And because it's real tldraw, you can grab any box, and keep editing.",
